## §C CONSTRAINTS

- Vite 7 + TypeScript 5.9 + `@evenrealities/even_hub_sdk` 0.0.15. npm, ESM, no framework.
- G2 canvas = 576x288 px, 4-bit greyscale (16 shades). ⊥ colour, camera, speaker. input = temple touchpad + optional R1 ring.
- dev server = `vite@<NAME>.service` (systemd, `Restart=always`), owns port `<PORT>`. ⊥ `npm run dev` by hand — 2nd process → `EADDRINUSE` or a stale instance the proxy hits instead.
- reverse-proxied at `/<NAME>/` by claude-hub. `base` in `vite.config.ts` ! = manifest `start_url`/`scope` = `.project-meta.json` `proxyPrefix`.
- `server.allowedHosts` ! ⊇ `.ts.net`. hub proxies `changeOrigin: false` ∴ upstream sees CLIENT `Host`; Vite 7 403s unknown hosts.
- delivery = live URL via `evenhub qr --url`. ⊥ `.ehpk` packing in the dev loop (store distribution only, & that build needs `--base=./`).
- service worker ⇒ secure context ∴ reach it over the **https** tailnet URL, ⊥ plain http from another device.

## §I INTERFACES

- url: `GET /<NAME>/` → companion page, through claude-hub. same url = Even App WebView target & PWA `start_url`.
- `src/glasses.ts`: `connectBridge(timeoutMs?) → EvenAppBridge | null`, `startGlassesPage(bridge, content) → GlassesSession {render, onTap, close}`
- `public/manifest.webmanifest` — `start_url`/`scope` `/<NAME>/`; `public/sw.js` — pass-through, scope `/<NAME>/`
- `app.json` — Even Hub manifest: `package_id` (lowercase alnum segments, ⊥ hyphens), `name` (≤20 chars), `permissions[]`
- card: `README.md` H1 → title, ¶1 → description, frontmatter `tags: [...]` → badges

## §V INVARIANTS

- V1: `base` in `vite.config.ts` = `/<NAME>/` = manifest `start_url` = manifest `scope` = sentinel `proxyPrefix`. any ≠ → assets 404 through the proxy, or the install scope drops the page it was installed from.
- V2: `server.allowedHosts` ⊇ `['.ts.net', 'localhost']`. ⊥ a concrete FQDN (commits the machine's tailnet name). loopback passes while the tailnet URL 403s ∴ test through the REAL url — the one the glasses load.
- V3: a bridge ⊥ proof of glasses. the SDK installs one on `window` in ANY browser & force-readies it after 100ms ∴ `waitForEvenAppBridge()` RESOLVES standalone; the host's absence shows up only in the first call across it — `createStartUpPageContainer` → non-zero, SDK logs "Flutter handler not available". ∴ detect companion-only from the RESULT CODE, ⊥ from the promise.
- V4: the companion page renders & the service worker registers BEFORE any bridge call. installability ⊥ depend on the glasses being present.
- V5: `public/sw.js` caches nothing. this page is a live view onto a dev server ∴ a cache serves a stale bundle to the glasses & reads as a code bug. add caching only w/ a versioned cache & a reason.
- V6: double-tap → `shutDownPageContainer` checked at the ROOT of the event handler, before the tap branch, whichever envelope carried it. it is the user's only exit.
- V7: tap/double-tap/lifecycle ← `event.sysEvent`; scroll ← `event.textEvent`. ⊥ mix. `CLICK_EVENT` is 0 & protobuf omits zero-valued fields ∴ the `?? CLICK_EVENT` default resolves INSIDE the envelope check — outside it, every scroll/exit/audio frame fires the tap handler.
- V8: `app.json` `package_id` = lowercase letters+digits per dot-segment, each starting w/ a letter; `name` ≤ 20 chars; `edition` = `202601`. `evenhub pack` rejects otherwise.
- V9: `README.md` H1/¶1/`tags` = the landing card's title/description/badges. ⊥ let them drift from §G.
- V10: still ⊥ top-level `await waitForEvenAppBridge()` — it can also never settle (no bridge object at all), which hangs the installed PWA blank. all bridge access goes through `connectBridge()`'s timeout race → `null`.
- V11: a host-less bridge is the NORMAL standalone case: `startGlassesPage` → `null`, page says "No glasses". ⊥ throw / render an error — that is what every plain-browser visit would show.

